  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'A sequence $(a_n)$ is said to converge to a limit $L$ if:', '["For every $\\varepsilon > 0$, there exists $N$ such that $|a_n - L| < \\varepsilon$ for all $n > N$", "$a_n = L$ for all sufficiently large $n$", "$(a_n)$ is bounded", "$(a_n)$ is monotonic"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The formal $\varepsilon$-$N$ definition of convergence: $a_n \to L$ means for every $\varepsilon>0$ there is $N$ such that $|a_n-L|<\varepsilon$ whenever $n>N$.', 'Sequences of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If a sequence $(a_n)$ converges, what can be said about its limit?', '["The limit is unique -- a sequence cannot converge to two different limits", "The sequence may have several different limits", "The limit must be zero", "The limit must equal the first term $a_1$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A standard theorem states that if a sequence converges, its limit is unique; a sequence cannot converge to two distinct values.', 'Sequences of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If a sequence $(a_n)$ converges, what can be said about whether it is bounded?', '["Every convergent sequence is bounded", "A convergent sequence need not be bounded", "Only sequences converging to 0 are bounded", "Boundedness has no relation to convergence"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A standard theorem: every convergent sequence is bounded (though the converse fails -- a bounded sequence need not converge).', 'Sequences of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Is every bounded sequence necessarily convergent?', '["No -- a bounded sequence need not converge (e.g. $a_n = (-1)^n$ is bounded but does not converge)", "Yes -- boundedness always implies convergence", "Yes, but only for sequences of positive terms", "No sequence can be bounded without also converging"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Boundedness is necessary but not sufficient for convergence: $a_n=(-1)^n$ is bounded between $-1$ and $1$ but oscillates forever without settling on a single limit.', 'Sequences of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'The Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem states that:', '["Every bounded sequence in $\\mathbb{R}$ has a convergent subsequence", "Every sequence in $\\mathbb{R}$ converges", "Every unbounded sequence has a convergent subsequence", "Every convergent sequence is monotonic"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem: every bounded sequence of real numbers has at least one convergent subsequence.', 'Sequences of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'A sequence $(a_n)$ is called monotonically increasing if:', '["$a_n \\leq a_{n+1}$ for every $n$", "$a_n \\geq a_{n+1}$ for every $n$", "$a_n = a_{n+1}$ for every $n$", "$a_n \\to \\infty$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A sequence is monotonically (weakly) increasing when each term is no smaller than the one before it: $a_n \leq a_{n+1}$ for all $n$.', 'Sequences of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Which of the following sequences is bounded but does NOT converge?', '["$a_n = (-1)^n$", "$a_n = 1/n$", "$a_n = n$", "$a_n = 2 + 1/n$"]'::jsonb, 0, '$a_n=(-1)^n$ takes only the values $\pm1$, so it is bounded, but it never settles near a single value -- it does not converge. $1/n \to 0$, $n\to\infty$ (unbounded, not convergent), and $2+1/n\to2$ (convergent).', 'Sequences of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'A geometric series $\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} ar^k$ (with $a \neq 0$) converges if and only if:', '["$|r| < 1$", "$r > 1$", "$r$ is any real number", "$a > 0$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A geometric series $\sum ar^k$ converges precisely when $|r|<1$, in which case it sums to $\dfrac{a}{1-r}$; for $|r|\geq1$ it diverges.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 1\left(\dfrac{2}{3}\right)^k$.', '["$3$", "$4$", "$1$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 2/3 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{1}{1-2/3} = 3$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 3\left(\dfrac{1}{4}\right)^k$.', '["$4$", "$5$", "$3$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 1/4 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{3}{1-1/4} = 4$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 6\left(\dfrac{1}{5}\right)^k$.', '["$\\frac{15}{2}$", "$\\frac{17}{2}$", "$6$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 1/5 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{6}{1-1/5} = \frac{15}{2}$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 2\left(\dfrac{1}{4}\right)^k$.', '["$\\frac{8}{3}$", "$\\frac{11}{3}$", "$2$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 1/4 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{2}{1-1/4} = \frac{8}{3}$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 8\left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^k$.', '["$32$", "$33$", "$8$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 3/4 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{8}{1-3/4} = 32$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 1\left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^k$.', '["$4$", "$5$", "$1$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 3/4 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{1}{1-3/4} = 4$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 7\left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^k$.', '["$28$", "$29$", "$7$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 3/4 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{7}{1-3/4} = 28$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 6\left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^k$.', '["$24$", "$25$", "$6$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 3/4 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{6}{1-3/4} = 24$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 9\left(\dfrac{2}{5}\right)^k$.', '["$15$", "$16$", "$9$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 2/5 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{9}{1-2/5} = 15$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 7\left(\dfrac{1}{4}\right)^k$.', '["$\\frac{28}{3}$", "$\\frac{31}{3}$", "$7$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 1/4 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{7}{1-1/4} = \frac{28}{3}$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 3\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)^k$.', '["$6$", "$7$", "$3$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 1/2 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{3}{1-1/2} = 6$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 2\left(\dfrac{2}{5}\right)^k$.', '["$\\frac{10}{3}$", "$\\frac{13}{3}$", "$2$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 2/5 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{2}{1-2/5} = \frac{10}{3}$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 3\left(\dfrac{3}{4}\right)^k$.', '["$12$", "$13$", "$3$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 3/4 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{3}{1-3/4} = 12$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the sum of the infinite geometric series $\displaystyle\sum_{k=0}^{\infty} 8\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)^k$.', '["$12$", "$13$", "$8$", "The series diverges"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $|r| = 1/3 < 1$, the series converges to $\dfrac{a}{1-r} = \dfrac{8}{1-1/3} = 12$.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'The $n$th-term test states that if $\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty} a_n \neq 0$ (or fails to exist), then the series $\sum a_n$:', '["Must diverge", "Must converge", "May converge or diverge -- the test is inconclusive", "Converges to 0"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The $n$th-term (divergence) test: if $a_n \not\to 0$, the series $\sum a_n$ necessarily diverges. (The converse is false -- $a_n\to0$ does not guarantee convergence, as the harmonic series shows.)', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'The harmonic series $\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \dfrac{1}{n}$:', '["Diverges, even though its terms $\\to 0$", "Converges to $1$", "Converges to $\\infty$ literally, as a finite real number", "Converges to $\\ln 2$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Despite $1/n \to 0$, the harmonic series diverges -- a classic example showing the $n$th-term test''s converse is false.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'The ratio test says that if $\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\left|\dfrac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\right| = L$, the series $\sum a_n$ converges absolutely when:', '["$L < 1$", "$L > 1$", "$L = 1$", "$L$ is any positive number"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The ratio test: $L<1$ gives absolute convergence, $L>1$ gives divergence, and $L=1$ is inconclusive.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If the ratio test gives $L = 1$ for a series $\sum a_n$, what can be concluded?', '["Nothing -- the test is inconclusive and another method must be used", "The series definitely converges", "The series definitely diverges", "The series converges conditionally"]'::jsonb, 0, 'When the ratio-test limit equals exactly 1, the test gives no information either way; convergence must be determined by another method.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'A series $\sum a_n$ is said to converge absolutely if:', '["$\\sum |a_n|$ converges", "$\\sum a_n$ converges but $\\sum |a_n|$ diverges", "$a_n \\geq 0$ for all $n$", "$\\sum a_n$ converges to a positive number"]'::jsonb, 0, 'By definition, $\sum a_n$ converges absolutely when the series of absolute values $\sum|a_n|$ converges.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'A series $\sum a_n$ is said to converge conditionally if:', '["$\\sum a_n$ converges, but $\\sum |a_n|$ diverges", "$\\sum |a_n|$ converges", "$\\sum a_n$ diverges", "$a_n \\to 0$ but nothing else is known"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Conditional convergence: the series itself converges, but taking absolute values destroys convergence, i.e. $\sum a_n$ converges while $\sum|a_n|$ diverges.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'The alternating harmonic series $\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \dfrac{(-1)^{n+1}}{n} = 1 - \dfrac{1}{2} + \dfrac{1}{3} - \dfrac{1}{4} + \cdots$ is an example of a series that:', '["Converges conditionally (it converges, but the harmonic series of its absolute values diverges)", "Converges absolutely", "Diverges outright", "Converges to 0"]'::jsonb, 0, 'By the alternating series test, $\sum (-1)^{n+1}/n$ converges (to $\ln2$); but $\sum |(-1)^{n+1}/n| = \sum 1/n$ is the divergent harmonic series, so the convergence is only conditional.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If a series $\sum a_n$ converges absolutely, must it also converge (in the ordinary sense)?', '["Yes -- absolute convergence always implies ordinary convergence", "No -- absolute convergence says nothing about ordinary convergence", "Only if all terms $a_n$ are positive", "Only if the series is geometric"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A standard theorem: absolute convergence implies convergence, i.e. if $\sum|a_n|$ converges then $\sum a_n$ converges too (the converse fails, as the alternating harmonic series shows).', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'By the comparison test, if $0 \leq a_n \leq b_n$ for all $n$ and $\sum b_n$ converges, what can be concluded about $\sum a_n$?', '["$\\sum a_n$ also converges", "$\\sum a_n$ must diverge", "Nothing can be concluded about $\\sum a_n$", "$\\sum a_n = \\sum b_n$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The comparison test: if $0\leq a_n \leq b_n$ and the larger series $\sum b_n$ converges, the smaller series $\sum a_n$ is squeezed into also converging.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'By the comparison test, if $0 \leq b_n \leq a_n$ for all $n$ and $\sum b_n$ diverges, what can be concluded about $\sum a_n$?', '["$\\sum a_n$ must also diverge", "$\\sum a_n$ must converge", "Nothing can be concluded", "$\\sum a_n = 0$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'If the smaller series $\sum b_n$ already diverges (grows without bound) and $a_n \geq b_n \geq 0$, then $\sum a_n$ must diverge as well.', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'A $p$-series $\sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \dfrac{1}{n^p}$ converges if and only if:', '["$p > 1$", "$p < 1$", "$p = 1$", "$p$ is a positive integer"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The $p$-series test: $\sum 1/n^p$ converges exactly when $p>1$ (e.g. $\sum 1/n^2$ converges), and diverges for $p\leq1$ (the case $p=1$ is the divergent harmonic series).', 'Series of Real Numbers', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If $\vec r(t) = f(t)\vec i + g(t)\vec j + h(t)\vec k$, the derivative $\vec r''(t)$ is defined as:', '["$f''(t)\\vec i + g''(t)\\vec j + h''(t)\\vec k$, i.e. differentiate each component separately", "$f(t)g(t)h(t)$", "The scalar $\\sqrt{f''(t)^2+g''(t)^2+h''(t)^2}$ only", "$f''(t) + g''(t) + h''(t)$ (a single scalar)"]'::jsonb, 0, 'A vector-valued function is differentiated componentwise: $\vec r''(t) = f''(t)\vec i + g''(t)\vec j + h''(t)\vec k$.', 'Differentiation of Vectors', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If $\vec r(t) = (- t^{2} + 4 t + 4, - 2 t^{2} - t - 1, 4 t^{2} + 2)$, find $\vec r''(t)$.', '["$(4 - 2 t, - 4 t - 1, 8 t)$", "$(5 - 2 t, - 4 t - 1, 8 t)$", "$(4 - 2 t, - 4 t - 2, 8 t)$", "$(- t^{2} + 4 t + 4, - 2 t^{2} - t - 1, 4 t^{2} + 2)$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Differentiating each component: $\vec r''(t) = (4 - 2 t, - 4 t - 1, 8 t)$.', 'Differentiation of Vectors', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If $\vec r(t) = (4 t^{2} + 3 t + 4, 4 t^{2} + t + 1, 2 t^{2} + 2)$, find $\vec r''(t)$.', '["$(8 t + 3, 8 t + 1, 4 t)$", "$(8 t + 4, 8 t + 1, 4 t)$", "$(8 t + 3, 8 t, 4 t)$", "$(4 t^{2} + 3 t + 4, 4 t^{2} + t + 1, 2 t^{2} + 2)$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Differentiating each component: $\vec r''(t) = (8 t + 3, 8 t + 1, 4 t)$.', 'Differentiation of Vectors', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If $\vec r(t) = (- 4 t^{2} - 3 t - 4, 4 t^{2} - 4, 3 t^{2} - 2 t + 1)$, find $\vec r''(t)$.', '["$(- 8 t - 3, 8 t, 6 t - 2)$", "$(- 8 t - 2, 8 t, 6 t - 2)$", "$(- 8 t - 3, 8 t - 1, 6 t - 2)$", "$(- 4 t^{2} - 3 t - 4, 4 t^{2} - 4, 3 t^{2} - 2 t + 1)$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Differentiating each component: $\vec r''(t) = (- 8 t - 3, 8 t, 6 t - 2)$.', 'Differentiation of Vectors', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If $\vec r(t) = (t + 3, - t^{2} - 4 t + 3, - 2 t^{2} + 3 t - 4)$, find $\vec r''(t)$.', '["$(1, - 2 t - 4, 3 - 4 t)$", "$(2, - 2 t - 4, 3 - 4 t)$", "$(1, - 2 t - 5, 3 - 4 t)$", "$(t + 3, - t^{2} - 4 t + 3, - 2 t^{2} + 3 t - 4)$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Differentiating each component: $\vec r''(t) = (1, - 2 t - 4, 3 - 4 t)$.', 'Differentiation of Vectors', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If $\vec r(t) = (- 4 t^{2} - 3 t - 3, - 2 t^{2} + 4 t + 3, - 4 t^{2} + 2 t + 2)$, find $\vec r''(t)$.', '["$(- 8 t - 3, 4 - 4 t, 2 - 8 t)$", "$(- 8 t - 2, 4 - 4 t, 2 - 8 t)$", "$(- 8 t - 3, 3 - 4 t, 2 - 8 t)$", "$(- 4 t^{2} - 3 t - 3, - 2 t^{2} + 4 t + 3, - 4 t^{2} + 2 t + 2)$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Differentiating each component: $\vec r''(t) = (- 8 t - 3, 4 - 4 t, 2 - 8 t)$.', 'Differentiation of Vectors', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'If $\vec r(t) = (- t^{2} + t - 3, 3 t^{2} + 4 t - 2, t^{2} + 3 t + 3)$, find $\vec r''(t)$.', '["$(1 - 2 t, 6 t + 4, 2 t + 3)$", "$(2 - 2 t, 6 t + 4, 2 t + 3)$", "$(1 - 2 t, 6 t + 3, 2 t + 3)$", "$(- t^{2} + t - 3, 3 t^{2} + 4 t - 2, t^{2} + 3 t + 3)$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Differentiating each component: $\vec r''(t) = (1 - 2 t, 6 t + 4, 2 t + 3)$.', 'Differentiation of Vectors', false, 'second', 2),
