  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the arc length of the curve $\vec r(t) = (1t, 1t)$ for $0 \leq t \leq 3$.', '["$3 \\sqrt{2}$", "$1 + 3 \\sqrt{2}$", "$\\sqrt{2}$", "$3$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $\vec r''(t) = (1,1)$ is constant, the speed is $|\vec r''(t)| = \sqrt{1^2+1^2} = \sqrt{2}$, and the arc length over $[0,3]$ is $\int_0^{3} \sqrt{2}\, dt = 3 \sqrt{2}$.', 'Line Integral w.r.t. Arc Length', false, 'second', 2),
