  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Find the arc length of the curve $\vec r(t) = (3t, 1t)$ for $0 \leq t \leq 3$.', '["$3 \\sqrt{10}$", "$1 + 3 \\sqrt{10}$", "$\\sqrt{10}$", "$3$"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Since $\vec r''(t) = (3,1)$ is constant, the speed is $|\vec r''(t)| = \sqrt{3^2+1^2} = \sqrt{10}$, and the arc length over $[0,3]$ is $\int_0^{3} \sqrt{10}\, dt = 3 \sqrt{10}$.', 'Line Integral w.r.t. Arc Length', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Set up the arc-length integral for $\vec r(t) = (t, \frac{t^{2}}{2})$ over $0 \leq t \leq 2$. Which integral correctly computes the arc length?', '["$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2 \\sqrt{1 + (t)^2}\\, dt$", "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2 (1 + t)\\, dt$", "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2 \\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\, dt$", "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2 \\sqrt{\\frac{t^{2}}{2}}\\, dt$"]'::jsonb, 0, '$\vec r''(t) = (1, t)$, so $|\vec r''(t)| = \sqrt{1+(t)^2}$, and arc length $= \int_0^{2} \sqrt{1+(t)^2}\,dt$.', 'Line Integral w.r.t. Arc Length', false, 'second', 2),
  ('mth-206-advanced-mathematics-vi', 'MTH 206: Advanced Mathematics VI', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Physical Sciences, Faculty of Engineering', 'Mathematics', '200 Level', 'Set up the arc-length integral for $\vec r(t) = (t, t^{2})$ over $0 \leq t \leq 1$. Which integral correctly computes the arc length?', '["$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\sqrt{1 + (2 t)^2}\\, dt$", "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 (1 + 2 t)\\, dt$", "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 t^{2}\\, dt$", "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\sqrt{t^{2}}\\, dt$"]'::jsonb, 0, '$\vec r''(t) = (1, 2 t)$, so $|\vec r''(t)| = \sqrt{1+(2 t)^2}$, and arc length $= \int_0^{1} \sqrt{1+(2 t)^2}\,dt$.', 'Line Integral w.r.t. Arc Length', false, 'second', 2),
